ull,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.056584029604184766,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":74.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.011591217688125766,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":64.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.08177,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":54.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Midland States Bancorp, Inc. operates as a financial holding company for Midland States Bank that provides various banking products and services to individuals, businesses, municipalities, and other entities. It operates in Banking and Wealth Management segments. The company offers commercial loans; commercial real estate loans that include various property types, such as owner-occupied offices, warehouses and production facilities, office buildings, hotels, mixed-use residential and commercial facilities, retail centers, multifamily properties, assisted living facilities, and farmland; construction and land development loans, including loans to small and midsized businesses to construct owner-user properties, loans to developers of commercial real estate investment properties and residential developments, and loans to individual clients for construction of single family homes; and residential real estate loans comprising first and second mortgage loans, and home equity lines of credit. It also provides commercial equipment leasing; depository products consisting of checking, savings, money market, certificates of deposits, and sweep accounts; and trust and wealth management products and services, such as financial and estate planning, trustee and custodial services, investment management, tax and insurance planning, business planning, corporate retirement plan consulting and administration, and retail brokerage services. The company was founded in 1881 and is headquartered in Effingham, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey G. Ludwig CPA | President, CEO & Vice Chairman | Age 53 | Compensation: $969,919 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 839 people. Revenue per employee of $387K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $143K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Midland States Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $660M market cap on $325M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding. Operating margins are contracting by -7.1pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $120M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 37 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"